---
description: Rules for implementing Figma designs with assets
alwaysApply: true
---

# Stack
- React 18 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS [v3 or v4 — specify]
- UI primitives in src/components/ui — REUSE, never regenerate
- Pages in src/pages, shared layouts in src/layouts
- Icons: lucide-react for generic; custom SVGs in src/assets/icons
- Images in public/images

# Required Figma MCP flow
1. Call get_metadata first to see the node tree
2. Call get_design_context on the specific target node
3. Call get_screenshot for visual reference
4. Inventory all assets BEFORE writing code
5. Extract assets, then write the component

# Asset rules
- Generic icons (arrow, check, menu) -> lucide-react, do NOT export
- Brand/custom icons -> src/assets/icons/[kebab-name].svg
- Illustrations -> src/assets/illustrations/[kebab-name].svg
- Photos/raster -> public/images/[kebab-name].[ext]
- Search existing assets before extracting — never duplicate
- SVG icons use currentColor so Tailwind text-* utilities work
- <img> always has width, height, alt

# Output rules
- Use Tailwind tokens, never arbitrary hex values
- Semantic HTML: button, nav, main, section, header
- Match Figma auto-layout to flex/grid + gap-*
- Preserve exact spacing, font sizes, weights, radius
- Include hover, focus, disabled states even if not in frame
- Stub click handlers with TODO — never invent logic

# What to avoid
- Inventing copy or icons not in the design
- Regenerating existing primitives in src/components/ui
- Adding dependencies without asking
- Embedding base64 image data in components
